From: SheepyLord <37598021+SheepyLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:40:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Merge upstream dxvk-remix main of 2026-11-14
 (remix-1.6.1..2b46bed0c)

Upstream NVIDIA dxvk-remix main at 2b46bed0c ("Merge branch 'dev/usdg_update_improvements'
into 'main'"): 57 commits since remix-1.6.1 (0a6cd5b1), applied with remix-1.6.1 as the merge
base, because patch 0001 already holds the fork's remix-1.6.1 merge. Upstream's fixes and
features come in whole: the core fixes 0091 ported (now present twice, identical), the eye
shading fixes, the bindless buffer, BLAS refit, decal/PSR, skinning and particle fixes, USDG
mesh packages (usdg.dll beside d3d9.dll), the water simulation, particle spawn distribution,
screen size and picking, the alpha blend dissolve, RTXDI's compact reservoirs (RTXDI dc8eb033)
and the Hydra AOVs.

Where both sides changed the same lines:
- Remix API 0.1000.2: upstream's struct types, the sludge bit and SetWaterSim and
  AddWaterDisturbance follow the fork's own (types 29-33, bit 28, slots 42-43); a 0.1000.0 or
  0.1000.1 client is written only the 41 functions it knows, and the new material texture
  transform fields are read only from 0.1000.2 clients (every fork version compares above
  upstream's 0.6.6 gate).
- remixapi_SetConfigVariable keeps calling readOption without an outer lock: the fork's
  readOption takes the option update mutex itself (patch 0029), so upstream's outer lock would
  deadlock.
- GPU layouts: the alpha blend dissolve mode sits in flags0 bits 3-5 (the texture flags'
  bits 19-30 hold the MMD alpha cutoff); upstream's camera material flags are opaque flag
  offsets 11 and 12 (6-10 are the fork's); a particle grows to 64 bytes, keeping the fork's
  float timeToLive at offset 44 and upstream's picking value at 48; RaytraceArgs and the
  particle constants gain a padded row; the particle bindings are 63-65.
- Emission is evaluated where upstream now does it, only for an emissive material, with the
  fork's legacy-emissive alpha mask, texture factor blend, sRGB textures, color tint and
  adaptive intensity (an adaptive material with a zero fixed intensity still emits).
- The spawn kernel keeps the fork's shelter relocation and landing trace, with upstream's
  surface-area triangle choice, uniform barycentrics and rejected spawns.
- The developer settings moved to dxvk_imgui_development_settings.cpp with the fork's FSR
  pass entry and its layer lock; the texture thumbnails keep the fork's per-frame
  registration with upstream's nearest-magnification sampler.
- Eye options: upstream's irisDepthScale and limbalRingScale replace irisDepth; the fork's
  sourceIrisSizeAdjustment stays. The eye override takes the fork's EyeRefract flag as a
  parameter (upstream's new signature has no Surface), and the EyeRefract iris also hides
  where the view ray does not reach it through the cornea.

Beyond the conflicts, to build and to pass the unit tests: the capture switch lists the
fork's LegacyEmissive and MmdAlpha categories; visibility reads the subsurface index through
the fork's getter; the sludge water material passes the fork's EnableTransmissionMask; the
fork's USD value reader takes float2 values, and texture transforms clamp an infinite
authored value to their limit as upstream's do; the particle constants are 464 bytes; the
thin-walled override patches the optional material copy. Upstream's API version test checks
the fork's line (0.1000.0 and 0.1000.1 clients keep their 328 bytes, stock 0.6.x clients are
refused); its camera material, particle picking and the fork's MMD alpha tests use the
merged signatures and layouts. RtxOptions.md is regenerated from the build (57 of 58 unit
tests pass; test_remix_categories cannot load d3d9.dll in its process, as before).

